<h2>Header, footer and logo</h2>

<p>
  The bar at the bottom of this very slide is the deck's <b>footer</b>. Define a <c>header</c> and/or a
  <c>footer</c> in <c>deck.json</c>: each has a <c>left</c>, <c>center</c> and <c>right</c> slot holding text, images, or a list of both.
</p>

<code lang=jsonc>
  "footer": {
    "left": ["logo.svg", "ACME Corp · Confidential"],
    "right": "{slide} / {slides}",
    "height": 42, "border": true,
    "background": "#0b1d2a", "color": "#9db4c0"
  }
</code>

<p>
  Text can use <c>{slide}</c> <c>{slides}</c> <c>{title}</c> <c>{slideTitle}</c> <c>{author}</c> <c>{date}</c>. A slot value that ends in
  <c>.svg</c> <c>.png</c> <c>.jpg</c> <c>.webp</c> is an image, relative to the deck folder. Bars are hidden on <c>layout: cover</c>
  slides unless you set <c>"cover": true</c>; any slide can opt out with <c>footer: off</c> or <c>header: off</c>.
</p>

<notes>
  Typical use: a school or company theme. Put the logo in the footer or header, add the name and the slide number.
</notes>
